<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">halberdier</ansi>

The Halberdier is a polearm fighter who wins by crowding. Its glaive strikes
past the front, and its Sweep cuts several foes with one swing, so a company
facing a packed row loses its enemies faster than a single-target fighter
could cut them down. Against a lone foe it is a plain, sturdy fighter. It is
a neutral class: it has no alignment gate to meet.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What the Halberdier is</ansi>

  Health      7 to start, 0.9 a level to level 20 (<ansi fg="command">help health</ansi>)
  Skill       Attack 1 and Evasion 0.9 a level (<ansi fg="command">help evasion</ansi>)
  Gear        medium armor, no shield, a glaive or a spear (<ansi fg="command">help armor</ansi>)
  Stats       strength 4, vitality 3, speed 2, perception 1 (<ansi fg="command">help growth</ansi>)
  Starts with the Polearm skill, which its abilities draw on
  Starter kit a glaive, a tunic, leggings, food, a waterskin and a knapsack

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How a Halberdier fights</ansi>

A Halberdier's strategy rule is <ansi fg="command">crowded</ansi> by default: it aims at the weakest foe
in the row with the most foes (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>). Its abilities need no command
and use no mana (<ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>):

  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Sweep</ansi>   one swing strikes its foe and the nearest foe beside it in the same
          row, each at 90% damage. From level 8 it strikes the whole row. It
          takes the whole turn and is ready again after 3 rounds. It is used
          when two or more foes stand in the target's row.
  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Brace</ansi>   from level 3, it holds its turn with the glaive set. The first foe
          that strikes into its place in the line is answered at once with
          a blow at 125% damage. If no foe strikes, the turn is lost. Used
          when Sweep is not ready (or has no second foe to strike) and a
          foe is striking at its place.
  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Hook</ansi>    from level 6, a glaive hit has a 20% chance (40% from level 20) to
          drag a leaping foe (a wolf, a hound, a spider) off its feet. A
          foe on the ground can't dodge or block.

Each Sweep blow is a real blow: it can miss, be dodged, blocked or parried,
and it can wound, which can break a chant (<ansi fg="command">help interrupts</ansi>). Turn abilities off
with <ansi fg="command">strategy [member] abilities off</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Routes</ansi>

At level 10 a Halberdier promotes to a Sweeper, a Vanguard or a Valkyrie. All
three are open at any alignment (<ansi fg="command">help halberdier-routes</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Companions</ansi>

A Halberdier companion fights the same way. Recruits are hired like any other
(<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>). Put them in the front or middle rank, facing rows of enemies:
the more foes in a row, the more a Sweep is worth.

Commands: <ansi fg="command">archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">class</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">strategy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help halberdier-routes</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help halberdier-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
